<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<!--
  =============================================================================
  The Aquarius desktop's right-click menu (labwc)
  =============================================================================
  Right-clicking the empty desktop opens this menu. rc.xml, next to this file,
  binds Root right-click to "ShowMenu root-menu"; this file is what root-menu
  contains.

  WHY THIS IS A labwc MENU AND NOT A SHELL-DRAWN ONE
    The shell draws its OWN menu off the Aquarius mark (components/bar/LogoMenu.qml)
    — that one can be a layer-shell popup because it hangs off a bar item the
    shell owns. The DESKTOP root is the compositor's, not the shell's, and there
    is no standard, compositor-agnostic way for a layer-shell client to be told
    "the user right-clicked the wallpaper at these coordinates" and to place a
    popup there. labwc's own menu is the right tool for a right-click on labwc's
    own root, and it is drawn by labwc from this file. On a different compositor
    the shell's mark menu and Super+Space still work; only this root menu is
    labwc's.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
    Desktop icons. Royce chose a clean desktop; this is only a context menu.
    Left-clicking the desktop still does nothing.

  THE ONE RULE THIS FILE OBEYS THAT MIGHT SURPRISE YOU
    NO COLOURS IN THIS FILE. This file is the menu's CONTENTS — what the items
    say and what they run. What the menu LOOKS like is written by a program:
    generate-theme, next to this one. It reads theme/Ice.qml or
    theme/Midnight.qml and writes out the card colour, the hairline, the text
    inks, the accent-tinted row under the pointer, the padding and the width,
    for whichever theme and whatever AQ_UI_SCALE are in force. The font is in
    rc.xml's <theme> section, because labwc splits colours and fonts across two
    files.

    There is no second copy of the palette anywhere, and there is no file to
    keep in step by hand. Before 2026-09-06 there was no design here at all and
    labwc drew this menu in its own default grey — the bench note "the right
    click menu does not have a design yet". The first fix that day was a
    hand-written themerc-override; the fix that replaced it, the same day, is
    the program. Do not tint anything here.

  Format reference: labwc-menu(5).
  =============================================================================
-->

<openbox_menu>
  <menu id="root-menu" label="Aquarius">

    <!-- The Aquarius search palette, the same message Super+Space sends. -->
    <item label="Search">
      <action name="Execute">
        <command>qs ipc call search toggle</command>
      </action>
    </item>

    <separator />

    <!-- The full Settings app, and its wallpaper page directly. `background` is
         a stable gnome-control-center panel id.

         WHY EACH ONE STARTS WITH `env XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=GNOME`, AND WHY IT
         IS NOT A TYPO. GNOME's Settings app checks which desktop it has been
         started under, and refuses to run under any it does not recognise. Its
         own source (shell/cc-application.c, is_supported_desktop()) reads the
         XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP environment variable, splits it on colons, and
         unless one of the names is "GNOME" or "Unity" it prints

             Running gnome-control-center is only supported under GNOME and
             Unity, exiting

         and stops, with nothing on screen. The Aquarius session sets that
         variable to aquarius-labwc:aquarius:wlroots on purpose — it is how
         xdg-desktop-portal finds aquarius-labwc-portals.conf, and changing it
         would silently break screen recording and file dialogs — so the fix
         belongs on the launch, not on the session. `env NAME=VALUE program`
         is the standard POSIX way to hand one program an altered environment
         and leave everything else alone. Take the prefix off either line below
         and that menu item goes back to doing nothing at all (bench, Royce,
         2026-09-06). The shell's own menu and Quick Settings do the same thing
         from QML, in one place: ../../services/SettingsLauncher.qml.

         ⚠️ THIS FILE HAS AN OS-SIDE COPY. What runs on an installed machine is
         system_files/usr/share/aquarius/labwc/menu.xml in the os-image repo;
         this one is what runs when the session is started from a clone of the
         shell. CHANGE ONE, CHANGE BOTH — the same rule the autostart file next
         to this one states, for the same reason. -->
    <item label="System Settings">
      <action name="Execute">
        <command>env XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=GNOME gnome-control-center</command>
      </action>
    </item>

    <item label="Change Wallpaper">
      <action name="Execute">
        <command>env XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=GNOME gnome-control-center background</command>
      </action>
    </item>

    <separator />

    <!-- Leave the session. This is labwc's own Exit, the SAME teardown
         Super+Shift+E runs (see rc.xml) — not a second way out. -->
    <item label="Log Out">
      <action name="Exit" />
    </item>

    <item label="Sleep">
      <action name="Execute">
        <command>systemctl suspend</command>
      </action>
    </item>

    <item label="Restart">
      <action name="Execute">
        <command>systemctl reboot</command>
      </action>
    </item>

    <item label="Power Off">
      <action name="Execute">
        <command>systemctl poweroff</command>
      </action>
    </item>

  </menu>
</openbox_menu>
